  "backstory": "He was once a sentinel of the High Peak, a dragonborn of brass scales and iron discipline who served as a sworn protector of the Sun-Touched Gates. For decades, his life was defined by the rhythmic clatter of the watch and the unwavering code of the Guard, a duty he performed with a stoicism that bordered on the divine. Yet, that life ended in a night of ash and betrayal when the citadel fell not to an invading army, but to an inner rot he had failed to see. As the flames consumed his kin and his station, the calm, measured breath of a soldier was replaced by a blistering, primal heat that surged from the depths of his draconic heart. He survived the slaughter by surrendering to a white-hot fury he never knew he possessed, carving a path through the ruin with a broken halberd and a voice that had forgotten how to speak in anything but a roar.\n\nStripped of his rank and his very identity, he abandoned his name to the embers of the gatehouse, believing himself unworthy of a title while those he was sworn to protect lay in the dust. He now wanders the borderlands as a nameless exile, his once-polished plate armor replaced by heavy furs and the scarred trophies of his survival. He did not choose the path of the barbarian; the path chose him when the structured world of law and order crumbled into chaos. His rage is not a lack of control, but a concentrated manifestation of his grief and his singular ideal: that no one else shall fall while he still draws breath. He is a shield that has forgotten its handle, a guardian who finds solace only in the visceral clarity of battle where the complexities of politics are replaced by the simple, brutal necessity of the strike.\n\nDriven by a flickering hope for redemption and the shadow of a bond he cannot let go—a promise made to a dying commander to find the architect of the citadel's betrayal—he moves toward the horizon. He seeks not gold or glory, but a weight to balance the scales of his soul and a reason to reclaim the name he cast aside. Until that day, he remains a ghost in tarnished brass, a silent sentinel who watches over the weak from the fringes of civilization. He is haunted by the flaw of his own perceived failure, a warrior who fears that if his rage ever truly cools, there will be nothing left of the dragon beneath the skin but cold, hollow stone.",
